[00:07.40] Charlie Freak had but one thing to call his own
[00:14.03] Three weight ounce pure golden ring no precious stone
[00:21.97] Five nights without a bite
[00:24.91] No place to lay his head
[00:28.94] And if nobody takes him in
[00:32.64] He'll soon be dead
[00:43.73] On the street he spied my face I heard him hail
[00:50.59] In our plot of frozen space he told his tale
[00:58.95] Poor man, he showed his hand
[01:01.85] So righteous was his need
[01:05.30] And me so wise I bought his prize
[01:09.53] For chicken feed
[01:20.22] Newfound cash soon begs to smash a state of mind
[01:27.31] Close inspection fast revealed his favorite kind
[01:34.85] Poor kid, he overdid
[01:37.77] Embraced the spreading haze
[01:41.83] And while he sighed his body died
[01:45.05] In fifteen ways
[02:02.18] When I heard I grabbed a cab to where he lay
[02:10.85] 'Round his arm the plastic tag read D.O.A.
[02:18.67] Yes Jack, I gave it back
[02:21.85] The ring I could not own
[02:25.63] Now come my friend I'll take your hand
[02:29.21] And lead you home
[02:39.54] 